# {{project_name}}

A MuduDB application written in Rust, packaged as `{{module_name}}.mpk`.
Scaffolded with [`mpm-crate`](https://github.com/ybbh/mududb_p) — edit this
project freely; it is a starting point, not a generated artifact.

It defines one table (`items`, see `sql/ddl.sql`) and one Mudu Procedure
(`create_item`, see `src/rust/procedures.rs`).

## Prerequisites

On PATH:

- `cargo` with the `wasm32-wasip2` target (`rustup target add wasm32-wasip2`)
- `cargo-make` (`cargo install cargo-make`)
- `mgen`, `mtp`, `mpm-build` — the MuduDB toolchain
- `mpm-install`, `mudud`, `mcli` — to install and invoke the package

## Layout

- `sql/ddl.sql` — database schema; `sql/init.sql` — seed data.
- `src/rust/procedures.rs` — hand-written procedures (`/**mudu-proc**/`
  marker; first parameter `xid: OID` is the transaction session).
- `src/rust/items.rs` — entity bindings generated by `mgen entity` from the
  DDL (run `cargo make generate` after editing `sql/ddl.sql`, and declare
  each new table file with `pub mod <table>;` in `src/rust/mod.rs`).
- `src/generated/` — async WASM wrappers produced by `mtp` (build artifact).
- `package/package.cfg.json` — package metadata; `package/package.desc.json`
  and `package/type.desc.json` are regenerated by the build.

## Build

```bash
cargo make package
```

This runs `mgen entity` → `mgen check-sql` → `mtp` (transpile + `mpm-build
merge-desc`) → `cargo build --target wasm32-wasip2 --release` → `mpm-build
create`, producing `target/wasm32-wasip2/release/{{module_name}}.mpk`.

## Install and invoke

Start `mudud`, then:

```bash
mpm-install target/wasm32-wasip2/release/{{module_name}}.mpk

mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc create_item \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "name": "pear"}'
```

## Extending

- Add a procedure: write another `/**mudu-proc**/` function in
  `src/rust/procedures.rs` and rebuild.
- Add a table: extend `sql/ddl.sql`, run `cargo make generate`, declare the
  new entity module in `src/rust/mod.rs`, then rebuild.
